// Things To Do
section#things-to-do.section.section-column.bg-800.context-dark
		.section-column-title.text-center
			.container( data-animate!={ class: 'fadeInUp' } )
				h6.text-primary Discover What Fiji Can Offer You
				h3 Things To Do
		.row.no-gutters.mt-0
			.col-lg-4.d-lg-flex
				.section-column-item.section-column-item-first.flex-lg-grow-1.bg-image( style='background-image: url("images/image-03-640x2000.jpg")' )
					.block.block-1.block-center( data-animate!={ class: 'fadeInUp' } )
						.badge.badge-primary Day 1
						h4 Arriving to Nadi, Fiji and starting your adventure.
						.offset-xs
							p You will be picked up at the Nadi International Airport and transferred to your accommodation for check-in. Then, you can enjoy the first ride towards the magnificent beaches. Leave Nadi’s Port Denarau at 8:45 AM to cruise on up to the stunning Blue Lagoon region.
			.col-lg-4.d-lg-flex
				.section-column-item.flex-lg-grow-1.bg-image( style='background-image: url("images/image-04-640x2000.jpg")' )
					.block.block-1.block-center( data-animate!={ class: 'fadeInUp', delay: '.15s' } )
						.badge.badge-primary Day 2
						h4 The Yasawas, Sawa-I-Lau Caves, and diving activities.
						.offset-xs
							p You will have the chance to experience the highlight of the Yasawas. Jump onto Joe´s Water taxi and join the tour to the Sawa-I-Lau Caves, where a short dive under takes you to a surreal underground cavern. After this amazing activity, return to the resort and feel free to enjoy other activities.
			.col-lg-4.d-lg-flex
				.section-column-item.flex-lg-grow-1.bg-image( style='background-image: url("images/image-05-640x2000.jpg")' )
					.block.block-1.block-center( data-animate!={ class: 'fadeInUp', delay: '.3s' } )
						.badge.badge-primary Day 3
						h4 Snorkeling with the reef sharks at the Yasawas.
						.offset-xs
							p With this tour, you’ll also have an amazing opportunity to snorkel with the reef sharks, afterwards enjoy the beach and all that this island has to offer to you! In the late afternoon, you'll board the Yasawa Flyer to head south to the Mamanucas. After that, an overnight in the Yasawas is planned.